;; Seon's own source as the program (session LOOP, seon.source tasks): which repository root
;; imports at boot and where merges that change it are committed.
;; Each entry's :default is its shipped value, with its unit,
;; provenance and what happens at its bound in the comment above it; a value read from the process (#env, a path
;; under the checkout, a #profile choice) is resources/seon/config/default.edn's (docs/config.md#layers).
{
 ;; Unit: path. The checkout the merge gate runs a merge's deferred process tests on
 ;; (seon.fx/run-tests: a worktree of it at the merges head, the candidate's files over it,
 ;; prove's entry there). Provenance: root's ruling (a), 2026-10-23, from step E's dry run (a test
 ;; root importing test/ could not host a checkout, and its gated merges were all refused).
 ;; Absent (as here): root's own source root (:seon.config.source/root as it resolves, the
 ;; standing root's merges tree, derived in the one merge of the layers, seon.config/layered), so every
 ;; root with a source gates a merge on the process tests its change reaches, nobody asking. With
 ;; neither (a test root given no source), such a merge is held, its reason naming the tests and
 ;; that no checkout runs them: never merged with them silently unrun.
 :seon.config.source/gate-checkout [:string {:seon.config/optional true :seon.config/place true :min 1 :seon.config/unit "path" :description "The checkout a merge's deferred process tests run on (a worktree of it at the merges head, seon.fx/run-tests): the standing root's merges tree. Absent: a merge reaching process tests merges with them unrun, an open problem until they run (root's git merge runs them, bin/prove)."}]
 ;; Unit: boolean. Whether a boot of a root with a source tree (:seon.config.source/root) catches main up with the files that changed
 ;; since main last indexed it (seon.system/catch-up, docs/source.md#a-boot-catches-up-with-its-checkout): about 40 ms when nothing
 ;; changed, the changed files' forms when some did. Provenance: the owner, 2026-11-10 ("if very little has changed it doesn't take
 ;; forever to start"); sessions edit the files from outside. False: the boot resumes main as it is and reads no file, for a Seon
 ;; no one edits from outside. At the bound: n/a.
 :seon.config.root/catch-up-on-boot [:boolean {:default true :seon.config/unit "boolean" :description "Whether a boot of a root with a source tree indexes the files that changed since main last indexed it (seon.system/catch-up); false: it resumes main as it is, reading no file."}]
 ;; Unit: boolean. Whether a merge writes its files and commits :seon.config.source/branch by itself. False: main is the source of truth, and
 ;; my.root/write-back! (seon_write_back) syncs main's changed files and commits, called by hand (owner, 2026-11-07). At the bound: n/a.
 :seon.config.source/write-back-on-merge [:boolean {:default true :seon.config/unit "boolean" :description "Whether a merge writes its files and commits the merges branch by itself; false: my.root/write-back! does, by hand."}]
 :seon.config.source/root [:string {:seon.config/optional true :seon.config/place true :min 1 :seon.config/unit "path" :description "The repository whose dirs main imports at boot (when main holds none of them) and whose merges branch receives the write-back; absent: no source is imported or written."}]
 ;; Unit: path, relative to the source root. Where the tree keeps its task files: a fact of the tree's layout, what a reader of a
 ;; tree's task files at a commit takes (bin/check's health step, test-runner/tasks-dir), never a process's place. A root's own
 ;; task dir is :seon.config.root/tasks-dir (the same path under the checkout by default; a check run's root takes its run's own).
 :seon.config.source/tasks-dir [:string {:default "resources/seon/tasks" :min 1 :seon.config/unit "path" :description "Where the tree keeps its task files, relative to the source root: a fact of the tree's layout, what a reader of the tree's task files at a commit takes (the health step), never a root's place (:seon.config.root/tasks-dir). See docs/tasks.md#task-files."}]
 ;; Unit: paths under the root, read in this order. Their .clj files are namespaces; the .edn
 ;; files under resources/seon/schemas are schema resources (schemas are program: an agent
 ;; changes one with my.schema/register!, and the merge writes it back; owner 2026-10-21).
 ;; test/ is in: a task's proofs and their fixtures live there, and an agent holds main's
 ;; tests only when main imported them (step E run #11, 2026-10-23: a worktree root without
 ;; test/ forked a design whose proof namespace did not exist, 27 turns of no progress). Only
 ;; a root with a source root imports (bin/system's: SEON_SOURCE_ROOT); a test's root states its
 ;; own dirs. It costs each boot the test forms' evaluation (+5 s a restart, measured
 ;; 2026-10-22; task seon.source/test-namespaces-built-into-the-binary).
 :seon.config.source/dirs [:vector {:default ["src" "test" "resources/seon/schemas" "resources/seon/config" "bin"] :seon.config/place true :seon.config/unit "paths" :description "The source directories under the root that are the program, relative to it."} [:string {:min 1}]]
 ;; Unit: {path pattern, kind}. The allow-list of the files under the dirs above that are facts of the program and not namespaces: a kind is how seon.source
 ;; reads and draws the file, a pattern a path whose one * stands for any name in that directory. Read by the import, the merge and the write-back
 ;; (seon.config/file-kind). Provenance: the owner, 2026-11-07: "an allow list with patterns seems like a good idea". At the bound: a file no pattern
 ;; names, under the dirs or not, is an ordinary file: no branch holds it and no merge carries it.
 :seon.config.source/things [:map-of {:default {"resources/seon/schemas/*.edn" :schema "resources/seon/config/default.edn" :config "bin/*" :script "test/seon/*.edn" :fixture} :seon.config/unit "{path pattern, kind}" :description "The allow-list of files that are facts of the program and not namespaces: each pattern, a path whose one * stands for any name in that directory, gives its file's kind (seon.config/file-kind). A fixture is a data file a test reads (my.branch/file), held as a file fact so it is in the program its test's digest covers."} :string [:enum :schema :config :script :fixture]]
 ;; Unit: paths under the root, of those above. The program proper: a namespace whose file is under
 ;; one is the program's, one under test/ (a test's, a fixture's, a helper's like seon.check or
 ;; seon.fixtures, whose names do not end in -test) is not (seon.program/program-nss). Read where
 ;; the program is told from its tests: the failure-point law's sites (a namespace with no file,
 ;; an agent's REPL app, is no failure point). Provenance: root, 2026-10-25 (the live round
 ;; 5's big-map request, whose nearest functions were test/ helpers). At the bound: an empty
 ;; vector makes nothing the program's (no law site).
 :seon.config.source/program-dirs [:vector {:default ["src"] :seon.config/unit "paths" :description "Of the source directories, those holding the program proper rather than its tests: a namespace whose file is under one is the program's."} [:string {:min 1}]]
 ;; Unit: qualified var names. A test whose reach (seon.program/graph-index, the compiler's
 ;; facts) references one of these reaches a process of Seon's own: an agent (in-agent), a fork
 ;; (lib/fork!), the binary or a root booted for it (binary-sh, through which ts/start-root!
 ;; starts every test root). Such tests run when named or in a merge's verification (bin/prove
 ;; --merge), not in a plain bin/prove (owner, 2026-10-23; root's ruling 2026-10-22: by the reach
 ;; walk, never a hand tag). A shell (clojure.java.shell/sh) is no such process: a git, perl or
 ;; mkfifo call costs milliseconds, and naming sh here left main-test's laws out of every plain
 ;; prove (audit 2026-10-26, item 7). Provenance: step E's run 4, where a turn's tests booted
 ;; roots and spun for minutes in an agent's fork; process tests were 782 s of 917 s of recorded
 ;; test time (pure-tests, 2026-10-23). A var missing here makes its tests run automatically
 ;; (slower, never wrong).
 ;; seon.cost-test/measure-unit starts no process, but measure or reload the runtime
 ;; they run on, which is bin/test's and not the built binary an agent's test child forks from: those proofs run at the gate.
 :seon.config.source/process-vars [:set {:default #{seon.agent-test/in-agent seon.cost-test/measure-unit seon.lib/fork! seon.test-store/binary-sh} :seon.config/unit "vars" :description "The vars through which a test reaches a process of its own (a shell, a fork, a root, the binary): a test whose reach references one is a process test, never run automatically, only when named."} :qualified-symbol]
 ;; Unit: vars. What the processes a test starts run for it: a form using a process var or a binary
 ;; var reaches them. seon.server/op-answer, the server's answer, a multimethod on a request's :op:
 ;; a form reaches only the methods of the ops it sends (its :form/ops), so a change to the :done
 ;; answer moves the tests that send :done and no other. seon.turn/work! is the agent's turn loop,
 ;; which root sends an agent as a quoted form, which no reference shows. Provenance: ctx-atom's
 ;; evidence (2026-10-27): seon.server-test's in-agent tests kept one reach digest across two fixes
 ;; to code their agent runs. Not seon.main/-main (1,512 vars): a root's boot is every process
 ;; test's, so each change deferred all 116 to the merge (owner, 2026-10-27: "no tests should
 ;; include all of src … the daily full run is the net"); a change to the boot alone is the merge's
 ;; run's and the daily run's to catch.
 ;; The owner, 2026-11-09, after two false greens (jolt/hiccup's render points and jolt/sync's answer to an agent stayed green
 ;; at their digests with the fix removed, their code reached only inside the agent's process): the agent's process entry,
 ;; seon.repl/serve! (its Flow graph: transport, repl, tests, render), is an entry too, so a change to what an agent's process
 ;; runs moves the digest of the process tests that reach it.
 :seon.config.source/process-entry [:set {:default #{seon.server/op-answer seon.turn/work! seon.repl/serve!} :seon.config/unit "vars" :description "What the processes a test starts run for it: the server's answer (a multimethod on a request's :op, of which a form reaches only the methods of the ops it sends, its :form/ops) and the agent's turn loop, which root sends the agent as a quoted form; not a root's boot, which is every process test's. A form that uses a process var or a binary var has a reach edge to each (seon.program/reach-step), where a request over a socket and a quoted form would leave it out."} :qualified-symbol]
 ;; Unit: submodule paths. The runtime every test, and every check step's contract key, runs on:
 ;; Jolt (its host layer, clojure.core and analyzer, which 970 of 977 tests reach) and Chez under it;
 ;; the binary and the test runner are built from them. Their gitlinks (a dirty submodule's files as
 ;; they are, seon.fx/pin) are in :env, so a bump of either re-runs every test once (about 5 minutes
 ;; for the non-process set). Measured 2026-10-29: seon.cost-test/the-unit-table-is-current stayed
 ;; green across a Jolt pin that moved its numbers, its digest unmoved. Replaces root's ruling D
 ;; (2026-10-27), which gave the runtime core no pin to spare reruns (Jolt bumped 15 times in 3 days)
 ;; and left a change there to the forks' suites and the full run, and the Jolt source groups it keyed
 ;; (analyzer, IR, deps, nREPL, core.async), which a pin in every digest subsumes.
 :seon.config.source/runtime-pins [:set {:default #{"reference-code/jolt" "reference-code/chez"} :seon.config/unit "submodule paths" :description "The submodules the runtime every test and contract key runs on is built from (Jolt, Chez): their gitlinks (a dirty one's files as they are) are in every digest's :env (seon.fx/inputs), so a bump re-runs every test once. See docs/source.md#tests-run-by-reach."} [:string {:min 1}]]
 ;; Unit: namespace prefix -> submodules. The libraries a test takes the pin of by what its reach
 ;; references (the namespace's own library and the libraries it runs on): a datahike bump reruns the
 ;; tests that reach datahike.*, not every test. Each submodule is a class (seon.config/pin-class),
 ;; taken by reach alone, by a test that reads files or runs a process too; lmdb and zstd by
 ;; konserve.jolt.lmdb and konserve.jolt.zstd, llama.cpp by seon.vector, awesome-jolt by none.
 ;; Provenance: root's task (2026-10-27): pins moved every digest in 3 of the last 12 --merge
 ;; batches (datahike 3, konserve 2, jolt 2).
 :seon.config.source/pin-namespaces [:map-of {:default {datahike #{"reference-code/datahike" "reference-code/konserve" "reference-code/persistent-sorted-set"
             "reference-code/jolt-fressian" "reference-code/jolt-overlay"}
  konserve #{"reference-code/konserve" "reference-code/jolt-fressian"}
  seon.vector #{"reference-code/llama.cpp"}
  awesome-jolt #{"reference-code/awesome-jolt"}
  malli #{"reference-code/malli"}
  konserve.jolt.lmdb #{"reference-code/lmdb"}
  konserve.jolt.lmdb-ffi #{"reference-code/lmdb"}
  konserve.jolt.zstd #{"reference-code/zstd"}
  jolt.crypto #{"reference-code/crypto"}
  org.replikativ.persistent-sorted-set #{"reference-code/persistent-sorted-set"}
  me.tonsky.persistent-sorted-set #{"reference-code/persistent-sorted-set"}
  fress #{"reference-code/jolt-fressian"}
  hasch #{"reference-code/jolt-overlay"}
  clojure.spec #{"reference-code/jolt-overlay"}} :seon.config/unit "namespace prefix -> submodules" :description "The submodules (reference-code/NAME), the code of a namespace prefix runs on, its own and its dependencies: a form referencing a namespace under a prefix has a test take those classes (seon.config/pin-class, a :seon.pin/* entry of :config, seon.fx/inputs). A submodule no prefix names and no :seon.config.source/runtime-pins holds takes no pin. A library used through interop or a :require with no var reference is not seen (the daily full run is the net)."} :symbol [:set :string]]
 ;; Unit: vars. The vars through which a test reaches the built binary (target/seon): a test whose
 ;; reach references one runs it, so bin/test builds it first; a process test that only shells
 ;; out (git) does not. Provenance: root's task seon.check/a-run-builds-the-binary-only-when-
 ;; something-reaches-it (2026-10-23): bin/test built it (46 s) whenever anything ran. A var
 ;; missing here is a missed build (a test fails on a stale binary), so it names the one way a
 ;; test starts the binary: seon.test-store/binary-sh, and seon.vector/start!, which execs
 ;; `target/seon embed-worker` (2026-10-29: the helper tests ran a stale binary, red and green at one
 ;; digest, until this named it).
 ;; seon.test-store/process-store (2026-10-29): a test that reads the process store's path needs the store
 ;; bin/test's plan makes, and the program bin/test seeds on it (seon.system/seed-program!), though it starts
 ;; no process itself (test-store-test's a-test-root-is-its-own failed with no-process-store when only it ran).
 :seon.config.source/binary-vars [:set {:default #{seon.test-store/binary-sh seon.test-store/process-store seon.vector/start!} :seon.config/unit "vars" :description "The vars through which a test reaches the built binary (target/seon): a test whose reach references one needs it built from the tree, so bin/test builds it first; nothing else triggers a build."} :qualified-symbol]
 :seon.config.source/tree-excludes [:vector {:seon.config/unit "paths" :description "Top-level paths of the checkout left out of its tree id (seon.fx/tree-id, bin/tree): none is read by a test or the build, so a commit to one moves no digest and rebuilds nothing."} [:string {:min 1}]]
 ;; Unit: branch. Git's main, which worktree branches merge into: a branch's health step reads
 ;; what it caused since its merge base with it (seon.fx/base-commit; root's ruling,
 ;; 2026-10-23). At the bound: n/a.
 :seon.config.source/main [:string {:default "main" :seon.config/place true :min 1 :seon.config/unit "branch" :description "Git's main branch, the one worktree branches merge into: a branch's health is what it caused since its merge base with it (seon.fx/base-commit)."}]
 :seon.config.source/branch [:string {:seon.config/place true :min 1 :seon.config/unit "branch" :description "The git branch of the root each merge that changes the source is committed on (never main, never pushed)."}]
 ;; Unit: a git identity. Seon authors and commits its merges (the message names the merged
 ;; tasks and runs). Stated here because a root's HOME is its checkout's target/home, which
 ;; holds no git identity (bin/check loop, 2026-10-21: "Author identity unknown").
 :seon.config.source/committer-name [:string {:default "Seon" :min 1 :seon.config/unit "name" :description "The author and committer of Seon's commits on the merges branch."}]
 :seon.config.source/committer-email [:string {:default "seon@localhost" :min 1 :seon.config/unit "email" :description "The email of Seon's commits on the merges branch."}]
 :seon.config.source/generations-dir [:string {:seon.config/place true :min 1 :seon.config/unit "path" :description "Where each generation is built: <dir>/<commit>, a worktree of the merges commit whose target/seon the next root runs."}]
 :seon.config.source/tests-dir [:string {:seon.config/place true :min 1 :seon.config/unit "path" :description "Where a merge's deferred process tests run: <dir>/<sha>-<uuid>, a worktree of the merges head with the candidate's files, removed after; its log beside it."}]}
